# QA (M2, fixed in E13 by D-050): coyote time at a water edge. Water used
# to kill on the first sub-pixel of the fall (the tiles sit flush with the
# walking surface), so the 6 coyote frames never applied over water. Now
# water kills once the feet have sunk player.water_sink_px (8) into it.
# Steps: Brunnwinkl relaxed opening (Mozartkugel, boulder, walker stomp),
# then walk right off the forest path towards the mill race (cols 43-44).
# Step 913 is the first airborne frame (feet 0.3 px below the path top);
# JUMP in step 914 (2nd coyote frame) jumps, she clears the 2-tile race and
# lands at step 958 (x >= 730, no death). Without the jump she would sink
# and die at 919. (The original bug report's step comments were 14 frames
# off; the "R 40" before the edge is now "R 26" so the press hits 914.)
level  = brunnwinkl
seed   = 1
source = handwritten
expect = deaths=0 no_event=Died state=playing player_x>=730
---
R 150
RJ 30
R 40
- 10
RJ 24
R 30
- 20
RJ 20
- 40
R 30
- 6
RJ 20
L 6
- 290
RJ 20
R 10
- 30
R 110
R 26        # on the edge of the path at step 912
R 1         # step 913: off the edge (should be coyote frame 1)
RJ 20       # step 914: JUMP within the coyote window
R 40
